            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "use empty string restriction value (see JCR 2700 and GlobPattern)",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=angela",
            "name": "angela",
            "key": "anchela",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Angela Schreiber",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2011-04-14T07:04:23.319+0000",
          "updated": "2011-04-14T07:04:23.319+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12503806/comment/13019714",
          "id": "13019714",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=tripod",
            "name": "tripod",
            "key": "tripod",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636"
            },
            "displayName": "Tobias Bocanegra",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Tokyo"
          },
          "body": "from JCR-2700:\n\n> an empty string restriction forces the ACE to take effect on the node it has been applied. \n\nwhich means in this case, effect on '/'. but if i want to restrict the subnodes of '/' i can't express this. but i can for all other nodes than '/'.\n\neg: using '/*' works but not on '/' which is not intuitive.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=tripod",
            "name": "tripod",
            "key": "tripod",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636"
            },
            "displayName": "Tobias Bocanegra",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Tokyo"
          },
          "created": "2011-04-14T07:42:55.554+0000",
          "updated": "2011-04-14T07:43:22.842+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12503806/comment/13019731",
          "id": "13019731",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=angela",
            "name": "angela",
            "key": "anchela",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Angela Schreiber",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "i see... interpreted your initial comment \"i tried to define a ACL on '/' that would allow 'read' on '/' itself, but not for the nodes underneath\" that you want to allow READ on '/' and only '/'. but what you want is \"deny READ to subnodes of '/' but not '/'.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=angela",
            "name": "angela",
            "key": "anchela",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Angela Schreiber",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2011-04-14T08:33:15.372+0000",
          "updated": "2011-04-14T08:33:15.372+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12503806/comment/13019891",
          "id": "13019891",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=tripod",
            "name": "tripod",
            "key": "tripod",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636"
            },
            "displayName": "Tobias Bocanegra",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Tokyo"
          },
          "body": "yes. the desired, effective result should be:\n- \"everyone\" allow read \"/\" (and it's properties ?)\n- \"everyone\" deny read \"/*\" (all subnodes of \"/\")",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=tripod",
            "name": "tripod",
            "key": "tripod",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=tripod&avatarId=17636"
            },
            "displayName": "Tobias Bocanegra",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Tokyo"
          },
          "created": "2011-04-14T16:22:02.858+0000",
          "updated": "2011-04-14T16:22:02.858+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12503806/comment/13019897",
          "id": "13019897",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=angela",
            "name": "angela",
            "key": "anchela",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Angela Schreiber",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "the properties get the permission inherited from the node unless there is a restriction matching specifically. \nthe jcr:read privilege currently is in our implementation not aggregated and thus does not allow to distinguish between different types of items.\n\nin other word: reading the node includes readability of it's property with the only exception that the jackrabbit extensions are used and the read access is narrowed by a pattern that only matches a subset of items (nodes or properties)",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=angela",
            "name": "angela",
            "key": "anchela",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
